  "details": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * kernel: udp: Deal with race between UDP socket address change and rehash (CVE-2024-57974)\n  * kernel: fuse: re-lock request before replacing page cache folio (CVE-2026-53388)\n  * kernel: net/handshake: hand off the pinned file reference to accept_doit (CVE-2026-63979)\n  * kernel: net/handshake: Drain pending requests at net namespace exit (CVE-2026-63978)\n  * kernel: fuse: re-lock request before returning from fuse_ref_folio() (CVE-2026-64266)\n  * kernel: net/handshake: Take a long-lived file reference at submit (CVE-2026-64523)\n  * kernel: ipvs: reload ip header after head reallocation (CVE-2026-68476)\n  * kernel: selinux: avoid sk_socket dereference in selinux_sctp_bind_connect() (CVE-2026-72242)\n  * kernel: KVM: s390: pci: Reject adapter interrupt forwarding if already enabled (CVE-2026-74515)\n  * kernel: usb: usbfs: fix use-after-free of usb_device in usbdev_release() (CVE-2026-80824)\n  * kernel: smb: client: clear setuid/setgid bit on write with cifsacl/modefromsid/posix extensions (CVE-2026-89638)\n  * kernel: vfio/pci: clear vdev->msi_perm after freeing it on init failure (CVE-2026-89777)\n  * kernel: md/raid5-ppl: fix use-after-free in ppl_do_flush() (CVE-2026-93262)\n  * kernel: KEYS: encrypted: fix integer overflow of datablob_len (CVE-2026-98222)\n  * kernel: netfilter: flowtable: hold reference on ct until flow is released (CVE-2026-98320)\n\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):  \n\n  * kernel panic at __crypto_xor+0x2 after a number of out-of-bounds read and use-after-free read (JIRA:AlmaLinux-257205)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
